---
import PageHeader from "@/components/PageHeader";
import SiteFooter from "@/components/SiteFooter.astro";
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — whatships.com"
  description="How whatships.com collects, curates, and presents product launch videos from X."
>
  <PageHeader active="about" client:load />
  <main class="about-page">
    <div class="about-content">
      <div class="about-intro">
        <h1>What is whatships.com?</h1>
        <p class="about-lead">
          An independent directory for discovering startup launch films,
          demos, and walkthroughs shared on X — built for useful browsing,
          not rankings, ads, or paid placement.
        </p>
      </div>
      <section>
        <h2>Why we built it</h2>
        <p>
          Great launch videos disappear into timelines within hours.
          whatships.com keeps a durable, searchable index so you can study how
          products announce themselves—and jump straight to the original post
          on X.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>What belongs in the index?</h2>
        <p>
          A video is published when it is clearly a product launch, demo, or
          first-look walkthrough with a public X post. Entries store product
          metadata, category, poster art, and a link back to the original
          tweet. Draft records stay offline until review.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Curation and submissions</h2>
        <p>
          The catalog is curated first. Anyone can propose a launch via the
          <a href="/submit/">Submit</a> form, which opens a prefilled GitHub
          issue for review. Approved entries are added to
          <code>src/data/videos.json</code> and published on the next site
          build.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Independence</h2>
        <p>
          whatships.com is not affiliated with X/Twitter or the products
          shown. Names, trademarks, and video content remain the property of
          their respective owners. Every profile links to the original post.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
